    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The inclusion criteria were: (1) Conformed to research questions, i.e., studies that estimated the reinfection rate of SARS-CoV-2 or we could calculate it based on the data provided in the paper; (2) The study design included cohort study, case-control study, and descriptive study; (3) The study fited our working definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection... reinfection working definition in this study was based on a positive laboratory result at least 90 days after laboratory confirmation of primary infection(laboratory testing methods include reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction or rapid antigen test, also called Lateral Flow Devices, and so on)...",
      "reason": "The eligibility criteria used to determine study inclusion are specified, including the research question component, eligible study designs, and follow-up/interval requirement via the reinfection working definition (≥90 days)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "To avoid language bias, the search was not limited to any language.",
      "reason": "Language restriction (no language limit) is stated, but dissemination year, and publication/report status (e.g., unpublished/ongoing) are not specified as eligibility criteria in the retrieved evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not distinguish exclusion of studies because outcomes were not measured versus because outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "Subgroup analyses were performed by meta-regression to fit stratified rates of reinfection based on variables such as variant and country, and we also used spline regression to fit time-varying reinfection rates that did not account for heterogeneity.",
      "reason": "The groups/stratifications used in syntheses (e.g., time-varying analysis; subgrouping by variant and country) are described, but the retrieved evidence does not explicitly link each synthesis group to specific comparisons defined in the review objectives."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_19",
      "quote": "first, we did not include the 'grey literature' , which may lack potential relevant studies that meet the inclusion criteria [35].",
      "reason": "A rationale is provided for at least one notable eligibility restriction (not including grey literature), but the retrieved evidence does not clearly provide rationales for all notable restrictions on study eligibility."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 74
}

